work-order.text:
{
  "acceptance": [
    {
      "check": "Signed-in user creates a group (name, currency, type) and sees it in the home group list with its per-group balance slot; opening a group they do not belong to (or that does not exist) returns an indistinguishable 404 with no data leak, and signed-out access redirects to sign-in.",
      "id": "AC-1"
    },
    {
      "check": "Missing-or-forbidden group reads are indistinguishable at the data layer: the membership guard returns 404 whether the group is absent, the caller is a non-member, or the id is malformed, and unit tests assert all paths carry no group fields.",
      "id": "AC-2"
    },
    {
      "check": "Owner copies an invite link; signed-in non-member B opens /join/<token> and claims placeholder 'Bo' as the join itself; owner rotates (old link dead) then disables (join rejected), each behind an explicit confirm naming the link; double-claim of 'Bo' is rejected.",
      "id": "AC-3"
    },
    {
      "check": "Remove-member, archive and leave flows each require an explicit confirm naming the object and succeed for zero-balance members; rename is not confirm-gated.",
      "id": "AC-4"
    },
    {
      "check": "Every group read and write is authorized on the server against the session user; negative matrix covered by tests.",
      "id": "AC-5"
    },
    {
      "check": "New screens use only ui.md tokens, keep one h1 with hierarchical headings, labelled controls with visible focus, and designed empty/loading/error states.",
      "id": "AC-6"
    },
    {
      "check": "Removal or leave with a non-zero balance is blocked with a message pointing at settle-up, and removal/leave paths call the zero-balance guard seam.",
      "id": "AC-7"
    },
    {
      "check": "Every membership change (join, claim-as-join, leave, remove) writes an ActivityEvent row with actor and timestamp in the same transaction as the change.",
      "id": "AC-8"
    },
    {
      "check": "A stale second claim of an already-claimed placeholder seat shows the seat-taken rejection on the join page; the seat stays with the first claimant and the loser is still offered a plain join.",
      "id": "AC-9"
    },
    {
      "check": "Renaming a group applies on save with a note and no confirm step; remove, archive, leave, rotate and disable keep their naming confirms.",
      "id": "AC-10"
    },
    {
      "check": "Remove/archive/leave success notes render at panel or page level (role=status) so the confirming form's unmount cannot take them with it.",
      "id": "AC-11"
    },
    {
      "check": "Opening the members screen while its data loads shows skeleton member rows and a loading invite-button state, streamed by a loading boundary.",
      "id": "AC-12"
    },
    {
      "check": "Rotating the invite link and then disabling it shows only the 'Invite link disabled.' note; the earlier 'New invite link created.' note is gone, because invite outcomes share one panel-level notice slot that each success replaces rather than stacks beside.",
      "id": "AC-13"
    }
  ],
  "alternatives_considered": [
    {
      "approach": "Client-only last-wins state in InvitePanel",
      "rejected_because": "Unpinnable under the node-only vitest contract and leaves two success slots for a future action to restack."
    }
  ],
  "approach": "Extend the proven redirect-with-notice mechanism to rotateInvite and disableInvite: each succeeds via Outcome/finish redirect to members?invite=rotated|disabled; the members page maps that single value to its sentence via a shared constant and InvitePanel renders it once at section level. A single query value makes stacking structurally impossible. Error paths stay inline.",
  "assumptions": [],
  "confidence": 85,
  "confidence_rationale": "Defect traced to a two-line site; fix reuses a pattern this ticket proves green three times; all new contracts assertable with existing test mocks.",
  "debate_summary": "v3 was incomplete, not wrong: BUG-3/BUG-4 verified fixed, but the invite panel — the last inline-success site in the same stale-notice family — was left untouched, producing PR-introduced BUG-5.",
  "evidence": [
    "error-context.md: rotate note count expected 0, received 1; snapshot shows sibling status nodes f2e16+f2e17",
    "groups-panels.tsx:301-305 two useActionState hooks, :369-370 two unconditional StateMessage renders",
    "actions.ts:467/495 inline success returns — last two actions off the Outcome/finish path",
    "qa-report attempt 2: BUG-3/BUG-4 fixed, single new fail T-13/BUG-5"
  ],
  "files": [
    {
      "action": "edit",
      "change": "Add INVITE_NOTICE_PARAM with closed rotated/disabled values, shared sentences, and inviteNoticeText mapper (null for unknown/blank).",
      "path": "lib/groups/validation.ts"
    },
    {
      "action": "edit",
      "change": "rotateInvite/disableInvite succeed via Outcome/finish redirect to members?invite=...; refusals stay inline; update module docstring.",
      "path": "lib/groups/actions.ts"
    },
    {
      "action": "edit",
      "change": "InvitePanel renders a single inviteNotice prop at section level; StateMessages remain for errors only; drop unreachable success effect.",
      "path": "components/groups-panels.tsx"
    },
    {
      "action": "edit",
      "change": "Members page reads the invite param via inviteNoticeText and passes it to InvitePanel.",
      "path": "app/groups/[id]/members/page.tsx"
    }
  ],
  "issue": 5,
  "kind": "feature",
  "mode": "committed",
  "out_of_scope": [
    "Group-detail/join cold-paint loading boundaries.",
    "Double-submit stacking on confirms.",
    "Favicon 404 noise."
  ],
  "qa_script": [
    "Rotate then disable behind naming confirms; assert only the disable note remains with zero rotate notes (T-13).",
    "Regression: old-link dead, disabled-link refusal, member bounce (T-3/T-4).",
    "Regression: remove/archive/leave notes, stale-claim, rename (T-5 through T-9)."
  ],
  "reproduced": true,
  "residual_risks": [
    "Notice query persists across refresh (accepted tradeoff)."
  ],
  "risks": [
    "Five bare-call rotate/disable test sites must switch to redirectUrl assertions in the same edit.",
    "Panel note must reuse exact sentences so T-13 getByText matches."
  ],
  "root_cause": "InvitePanel holds two independent useActionState hooks each rendering its own unconditional StateMessage, so rotate then disable successes coexist as sibling role=status nodes; rotate/disable were the last two actions still returning inline success, untouched by v3's redirect generalization.",
  "tests": [
    {
      "action": "edit",
      "cases": [
        "rotateInvite success redirects to members?invite=rotated",
        "disableInvite success redirects to members?invite=disabled",
        "rotate-then-disable leaves a single invite value",
        "refusals stay inline with no redirect",
        "existing bare-call sites updated to redirectUrl"
      ],
      "path": "lib/groups/actions.test.ts"
    },
    {
      "action": "edit",
      "cases": [
        "inviteNoticeText maps both values to exact sentences",
        "inviteNoticeText returns null for unknown/blank/undefined"
      ],
      "path": "lib/groups/validation.test.ts"
    }
  ],
  "understanding": "The previous plan (v3) was not wrong — BUG-3 and BUG-4 are verified fixed — but incomplete: it left the invite panel, the fourth inline-success site in the same stale-notice family, untouched. Two independent inline success slots stack rotate and disable notes (BUG-5). This order finishes the generalization with a single invite query value, making stacking unrepresentable.",
  "unknowns": [],
  "version": 4
}
